{"id":"4932fa2e649322cf","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-df-stable-distribution.md","title":"Stable Distribution","display":"df-stable-distribution — Stable Distribution","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-stable-distribution","aliases":["58-df-stable-distribution"],"display":"df-stable-distribution — Stable Distribution","depends_on":["[[../batch07/58-df-iid.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-borel.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-stable-distribution"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-stable-distribution</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-stable-distribution — Stable Distribution"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"64b5bf078722d744\" href=\"?note=64b5bf078722d744\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-iid.md\">../batch07/58-df-iid.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"9375de7089953a2b\" href=\"?note=9375de7089953a2b\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-borel.md\">../batch16/58-df-borel.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,X_\\bullet\\in V\">\\(X,X_\\bullet\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha\\in(0,2]\">\\(\\alpha\\in(0,2]\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IID}_S\\subseteq V^8\">\\(\\mathrm{IID}_S\\subseteq V^8\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"64b5bf078722d744\" href=\"?note=64b5bf078722d744\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-iid.md\">../batch07/58-df-iid.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\">\\(\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\\)</span> is the Borel sigma-algebra from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"9375de7089953a2b\" href=\"?note=9375de7089953a2b\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-borel.md\">../batch16/58-df-borel.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{StableDistribution}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\operatorname{StableDistribution}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}distribution} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{StableDistribution}_S(X,\\alpha) \\leftrightarrow\n0&lt;\\alpha\\leq2\\land\n\\exists\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mu,X_\\bullet\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{IID}_S(X_\\bullet,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))\n\\land X=X_\\bullet(0)\\land\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists b_n\\in\\mathbb R\\;\n\\forall A\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\sum_{k=1}^{n}X_\\bullet(k)(\\xi)\\in A\\}\\bigr)\n=\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:n^{1/\\alpha}X(\\xi)+b_n\\in A\\}\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}distribution} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{StableDistribution}_S(X,\\alpha) \\leftrightarrow\n0&lt;\\alpha\\leq2\\land\n\\exists\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mu,X_\\bullet\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{IID}_S(X_\\bullet,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))\n\\land X=X_\\bullet(0)\\land\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists b_n\\in\\mathbb R\\;\n\\forall A\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\sum_{k=1}^{n}X_\\bullet(k)(\\xi)\\in A\\}\\bigr)\n=\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:n^{1/\\alpha}X(\\xi)+b_n\\in A\\}\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Equality in distribution is expanded as equality of the two inverse-image probabilities on every Borel set, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> is the zeroth member of the displayed i.i.d. real-valued family.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha = 2\">\\(\\alpha = 2\\)</span> gives normal; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha = 1\">\\(\\alpha = 1\\)</span> gives Cauchy.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch07/58-df-iid.md","status":"resolved","id":"64b5bf078722d744","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-iid.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-borel.md","status":"resolved","id":"9375de7089953a2b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-borel.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-iid.md","status":"resolved","id":"64b5bf078722d744","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{IID}_S\\subseteq V^8$ (see [[../batch07/58-df-iid.md]]).","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-borel.md","status":"resolved","id":"9375de7089953a2b","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)$ is the Borel sigma-algebra from [[../batch16/58-df-borel.md]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,X_\\bullet\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\alpha\\in(0,2]","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{IID}_S\\subseteq V^8","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{StableDistribution}_S\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}distribution} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{StableDistribution}_S(X,\\alpha) \\leftrightarrow\n0<\\alpha\\leq2\\land\n\\exists\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mu,X_\\bullet\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{IID}_S(X_\\bullet,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))\n\\land X=X_\\bullet(0)\\land\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists b_n\\in\\mathbb R\\;\n\\forall A\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\sum_{k=1}^{n}X_\\bullet(k)(\\xi)\\in A\\}\\bigr)\n=\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:n^{1/\\alpha}X(\\xi)+b_n\\in A\\}\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"X","display":false},{"tex":"\\alpha = 2","display":false},{"tex":"\\alpha = 1","display":false}],"bytes":1445,"backlinks":[{"id":"e002586cbe5331e7","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{StableDistribution}_S$ (real-valued stable-distribution predicate, see [[../batch14/58-df-stable-distribution.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1216","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-stable-distribution.md|58-df-stable-distribution]]（batch14）"}],"outgoing":["64b5bf078722d744","9375de7089953a2b"]}